  doc = """
  Current production model (2035 standard): OptimaFormer-350M-2029 checkpoint (350 M params, trained on 8.7 × 10¹³ parameter-updates across 1.2 million distinct problems).

  Embedding properties that have proven necessary and sufficient:
  1. Smoothness: small changes in problem → small changes in Z
  2. Disentanglement: axes roughly correspond to human-interpretable concepts (modality, ruggedness, curvature scale, deceptiveness, conditioning, neutrality, separability, noise level)
  3. Hierarchical structure: first 512 dims = micro-structure (local curvature, noise), next 512 = meso (basins, barriers), last 512–1024 = macro (global topology, symmetry)
  4. Causal fidelity: interventions in Z (e.g. “make more rugged”) correspond to real increase in ruggedness when decoded)

  With this embedding, any new problem is solved in three steps:
  1) Encode → z ∈ Z  (takes ~8 ms on single A100)
  2) Nearest-neighbor lookup in policy library → retrieve top-k policies that worked on similar z
  3) Fine-tune / compose retrieved policies (usually <5 % adaptation needed)

  Observed transfer performance (2034 meta-analysis):
  • Zero-shot (direct reuse): 78 % of peak performance
  • 8-shot compositional adaptation: 96 % of peak
  • Full retrain baseline: 100 %
  """
  embedding_dim = 2048
  encoder_model = "OptimaFormer-350M-2029"
  training_tokens = 8.7e13
  zero_shot_success_rate = 0.78
  eight_shot_success_rate = 0.96
  confidence = 0.99
}
